  "simpleslabs.guide.page.1": "Half slabs - 4 pixels, half a slab - of every block with a slab: any of the four layers of a cell, upright against a wall as side half slab or side slab, cut in the Shapecutter and crafted back into the slab.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.2.title": "Half slabs: 4-pixel layers of every block with a slab",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.2": "A half slab is half a slab: 4 pixels high. Every block that has a slab (170:",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.3.title": "Half slabs: 4-pixel layers of every block with a slab",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.3": "Vanilla, SimpleBuilding and its sub-mods, also dirt, grass, sand, red sand and gravel) has its half slab with the textures of its slab.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.4.title": "Half slabs: 4-pixel layers of every block with a slab",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.4": "A block cell holds four layers, and any of them can be filled in any combination.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.5.title": "Side half slab and side slab",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.5": "Sneak + right-click on the side of a block puts the half slab upright against that side: a side half slab of 4 pixels. Each further sneak click on that block side, or a click on its open face, adds a layer:",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.6.title": "Side half slab and side slab",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.6": "2 layers are a side slab of 8 pixels, 4 layers fill the cell.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.7.title": "Slab and half slab in one block",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.7": "A half slab used on its own slab (bottom or top, not double) adds a layer: the slab becomes the half slab block with its two layers and the new one, water stays.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.8.title": "Breaking and water",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.8": "Breaking a half slab block drops one half slab for every filled layer. Half slabs hold water like a slab; a full cell (4 layers) holds none.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.9.title": "Sand, gravel and grass",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.9": "Sand, red sand and gravel half slabs fall like sand: with nothing below they fall as their layers and land at the bottom of the cell; on the ground their layers settle to the bottom.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.10.title": "Sand, gravel and grass",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.10": "One falling onto a half slab of the same kind fills it up, the rest goes into the cell above. The grass half slab takes the color of the biome and shows grass on its top layer, dirt below.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.11.title": "Copper half slabs age",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.11": "Unwaxed copper half slabs age like Vanilla copper: exposed, weathered, oxidized.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.12.title": "Copper half slabs age",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.12": "A honeycomb waxes them (they keep their look), an axe scrapes the wax or one stage off; a dispenser with honeycomb waxes too.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.13.title": "Shapecutter and back",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.13": "The Shapecutter of Simple Blocks cuts 2 half slabs from a slab and 4 from its full block; without Simple Blocks the Vanilla stonecutter does it.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.14.title": "Shapecutter and back",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.14": "Two half slabs craft back into one slab (nothing lost).",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.15.title": "Half slabs of other mods' blocks",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.15": "Half slabs of the blocks of SimpleBuilding, Simple Blocks, Simple End, Simple Ores, Simple Enchanting and Simple Chess exist only while that mod is loaded, with their recipes.",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.16.title": "Half slabs of other mods' blocks",
  "simpleslabs.guide.page.16": "Their properties come from SimpleLib's shape core, which Simple Octets uses too."
}
